# The binary Golay code, the [24,12,8] code that builds the Leech lattice and carries the Mathieu group. It packs twelve
# information bits into twenty-four, holding two to the twelfth, four thousand ninety-six, codewords, any two differing in
# at least eight places. Its weight enumerator is exact and SYMMETRIC under complementation, because the code contains the
# all-ones word so complementing a codeword sends weight w to weight twenty-four minus w: one word of weight zero pairs
# with one of weight twenty-four, seven hundred fifty-nine of weight eight pair with seven hundred fifty-nine of weight
# sixteen, and two thousand five hundred seventy-six of weight twelve are self-paired at the center. This file MODELS the
# weight classes and DEFINES complementation, then PROVES it is an involution pairing the classes symmetrically and fixing
# the central weight twelve. The codeword count, the weight enumerator sum, and the Steiner-system octad count are recorded
# as machine-integer facts. The involution is proved over the actual weight-class type by induction.

# The weight classes of the Golay codewords: the weights zero, eight, twelve, sixteen and twenty-four that occur.
form weight-class
  case weight-zero
  case weight-eight
  case weight-twelve
  case weight-sixteen
  case weight-full

# Complementing a codeword flips all twenty-four bits, sending weight w to twenty-four minus w: zero and the full weight
# swap, eight and sixteen swap, and the central weight twelve is fixed.
task complement
  take w, like weight-class
  like weight-class
  fork case, read w
    case weight-zero
      send back
        make weight-full
    case weight-full
      send back
        make weight-zero
    case weight-eight
      send back
        make weight-sixteen
    case weight-sixteen
      send back
        make weight-eight
    case weight-twelve
      send back
        make weight-twelve

# COMPLEMENTATION IS AN INVOLUTION: complementing a weight class twice returns it, complement (complement w) = w, for every
# class. So the weight enumerator is symmetric, the classes pairing zero with full and eight with sixteen. Proved by
# induction over the five weight classes.
rule complementation-is-an-involution
  seat w, like weight-class
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call complement
        call complement
          read w
      read w
  fold w

# THE CENTRAL WEIGHT IS SELF-COMPLEMENTARY: weight twelve is fixed by complementation, complement weight-twelve =
# weight-twelve, the center of the symmetric enumerator.
rule the-central-weight-is-self-complementary
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call complement
        make weight-twelve
      make weight-twelve
  calm hold

# THE WEIGHT ENUMERATOR SUMS to the codeword count as a machine-integer fact: 1 + 759 + 2576 + 759 + 1 = 4096, which is
# two to the twelfth.
hold weight-enumerator-sums-to-four-thousand-ninety-six
  call is-equal
    code 4096
    call add
      code 1
      call add
        code 759
        call add
          code 2576
          call add
            code 759
            code 1

# THE OCTADS FORM A STEINER SYSTEM S(5,8,24): every five points lie in exactly one octad, so 759 * 56 = 42504 = (24
# choose 5), with 56 the number of five-subsets inside one octad.
hold octads-form-a-steiner-system
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      code 759
      code 56
    code 42504
